{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-18-1","title":"Psalms 18:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 David praises God for his manifold and marvellous blessings.</p>\n<p>A.M. 2986. B.C. 1018. (Title.) the servant. 36:1; *title 116:16; 2Sa 22:1-51; Ac 13:36; Heb 3:5 in the day. 34:19; Ex 15:1-21; Jud 5:1-31; 1Sa 2:1-10; Isa 12:1-6 I will. 116:1-6; 144:1,2; 1Jo 4:19 my. 32; 28:7,8; 118:14; Isa 12:2; Php 4:13; Col 1:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-2","title":"Psalms 18:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Lord. 28:1; 62:2,7; Isa 32:2 fortress. 91:2; 144:2; Jer 16:19 strength. Heb. rock. whom. Heb 2:13 buckler. 91:4; Pr 2:7 horn. 132:17; 2Sa 22:3 high. Pr 18:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-3","title":"Psalms 18:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>I will. 5:2,3; 28:1,2; 55:16; 62:8; 2Sa 22:4; Php 4:6,7 who. 65:1,2; 76:4; Ne 9:5; Re 4:11; 5:12-14 so shall. 50:15; 91:15; Lu 1:71; Ac 2:21; Ro 8:31-39</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-4","title":"Psalms 18:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>sorrows. 116:3; 2Sa 22:5,6; Isa 13:8; 53:3,4; Mt 26:38,39; Mr 14:33,34 2Co 1:9 floods. 22:12,13,16; Jon 2:2-7; Mt 26:47,55; 27:24,25,39-44; Ac 21:30 ungodly men. Heb. Belial.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-5","title":"Psalms 18:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>The sorrows, or, cords. 86:13; 88:3-8,15-17; Ac 2:24 snares. Ec 9:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-6","title":"Psalms 18:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>distress. 3,4; 50:15; 130:1,2; Mr 14:36; Ac 12:5 heard. 5:7; 11:4; 27:4,5; 2Sa 22:7; Hab 2:20; Re 11:19 my cry. Ex 2:23; 1Ki 8:27-30; 2Ch 30:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-7","title":"Psalms 18:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>earth. 114:4-7; Mt 28:2; Ac 4:31; 16:25,26 foundations. 46:2; De 32:22; Jer 4:24; Eze 38:19,20; Hab 3:6,10; Zec 14:4 1Co 13:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-8","title":"Psalms 18:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>went. 11:6; 21:9; 74:1; 104:32; 144:5,6; Ge 19:28; Le 10:2; Nu 11:1; 16:35 De 29:20,23,24, 2Th 1:8 out of his. Heb. by his. fire. Da 7:10; Am 4:11; Na 1:5,6; Re 11:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-9","title":"Psalms 18:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>He bowed.Jehovah is here represented as a mighty warrior going forth to fight the battles of David. When He descended to the engagement, the very heavens bowed to render his descent more awful: His military tent was substantial darkness; the voice of His thunder was the warlike alarm which sounded to battle; the chariot in which He rode was the thick clouds of heaven, conducted by cherubs, and carried on by the irresistible force and rapid wings of an impetuous tempest; and the darts and weapons He employed were thunder-bolts, lightnings, fiery hail, deluging rains, and stormy winds! No wonder that when God arose all His enemies were scattered, and those that hated Him fled before Him.</p>\n<p>68:4; 144:5-15; De 33:26; 2Sa 22:10; Isa 51:6; Joe 3:16; Mt 24:29 Heb 12:26; 2Pe 3:10; Re 20:11 darkness. De 5:22,23; Mr 15:33; Joh 13:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-10","title":"Psalms 18:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>rode. 99:1; 2Sa 22:11,12; Eze 1:5-14; 10:20-22 he did fly. 104:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-11","title":"Psalms 18:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>secret. 27:5; 81:7; 91:1 thick. 97:2; De 4:11; Joe 2:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-12","title":"Psalms 18:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>At the. 97:3,4; Hab 3:4,5; Mt 17:2,5 hail. Ex 9:23,24; Jos 10:11; 2Sa 22:13-15; Re 16:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-13","title":"Psalms 18:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>thundered. 78:48; 104:7; Ex 20:18; 1Sa 7:10; Job 40:9; Joh 12:29; Re 4:5; 8:5 Re 19:6 Highest. 29:3,4; Eze 10:5 coals. 120:3,4; 140:10; De 32:24; *marg: Hab 3:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-14","title":"Psalms 18:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>Yea. 21:12; 77:17; Nu 24:8; De 32:23,42; Jos 10:10; Job 6:4; Isa 30:30 Hab 3:11 he shot. 144:6; Job 38:35; 40:9-12; Zec 9:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-15","title":"Psalms 18:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>channels. 74:15; 106:9; Ex 15:8; Jos 3:13-16; 2Sa 22:16 foundations. 104:5; Job 38:4-6; Jer 31:37; Jon 2:6; Mic 6:2 O Lord. 2Ki 19:7; Job 4:9; Isa 11:4; 30:27,28,33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-16","title":"Psalms 18:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>He sent. 57:3; 144:7 drew. 43; 40:1-3; Ex 2:10; 2Sa 22:17 many waters. or, great waters. Jon 2:5,6; Re 17:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-17","title":"Psalms 18:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>strong. 38:19; 2Sa 22:1,18; Heb 2:14,15 them. 40,41; 9:13; 25:19; 69:4-14; 118:7; Job 16:9; Lu 19:14 they were. 35:10; Eph 6:10-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-18","title":"Psalms 18:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>me in. De 32:35; 2Sa 22:19; Jer 18:17; Ob 1:10-14; Zec 1:15 but. 46:1,2,11; 1Sa 30:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-19","title":"Psalms 18:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>brought. 36; 31:8; 40:2; 118:5; Job 36:16 because. 37:23; 2Sa 22:18-27; 1Ki 10:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-20","title":"Psalms 18:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>rewarded. 58:11; 1Sa 24:17,20; Pr 11:18; Isa 49:4; 62:11; Mt 6:4; 1Co 3:8 cleanness. 24; 7:3; 24:4; 26:6; 1Sa 24:11-13; Heb 7:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-21","title":"Psalms 18:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>For I. 17:4; 26:1; 119:10,11; Ac 24:16; 1Th 2:10 have not. 119:102; 1Sa 15:11; 1Jo 2:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-22","title":"Psalms 18:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>For all. 119:13,128; Joh 5:14 I did. 119:112,117</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-23","title":"Psalms 18:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>upright. 7:1-8:9; 11:7; 17:3; 37:27; 1Sa 26:23; 1Ch 29:17 before. Heb. with. I kept. Mt 5:29,30; 18:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-24","title":"Psalms 18:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>the Lord recompensed me. Ru 2:12; Mt 10:41,42; 2Th 1:6,7; Heb 6:16 in his eyesight. Heb. before his eyes.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-25","title":"Psalms 18:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>With the. 41:1-4; 112:4-6; Ne 9:17; Isa 57:1,2; 58:7,8; Mt 18:33-35 Lu 6:35-38 thou wilt. Isa 26:7; Eze 18:25-30; Ro 9:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-26","title":"Psalms 18:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>froward. 109:17-19; Le 26:23,24,27,28; Pr 3:34; Ro 2:4-6,9; Jas 2:13 shew thyself froward. or, wrestle.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-27","title":"Psalms 18:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>save. 9:18; 34:6,19; 40:17; 2Sa 22:28; Isa 57:15; 66:2; Lu 1:52,53 2Co 8:9; Jas 2:5 bring. 10:4; 17:10,13; 101:5; Pr 6:16,17; 30:12; Isa 3:9; 10:12; Lu 18:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-28","title":"Psalms 18:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>thou wilt. 112:4; Job 18:6; 29:3 candle. or, lamp. 132:17; 2Sa 22:29; 1Ki 11:36; Pr 20:27; Isa 62:1 my God. Isa 42:16; Mt 4:16; Lu 1:79; 1Pe 2:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-29","title":"Psalms 18:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>by thee. 44:6,7; 144:1,10; 1Sa 17:49; 23:2; 30:8; 2Sa 5:19,20,25 Eph 6:10-13; Col 2:15; Re 3:21 run. or, broken. by my God. 2Sa 22:30; 1Co 15:10; 2Co 12:9,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-30","title":"Psalms 18:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>his way. 19:7; 25:10; De 32:4; 2Sa 22:31; Da 4:37; Ro 12:2; Re 15:3 tried. or, refined. 12:6; 19:8-10; 119:140; Pr 30:5 a buckler. 2; 17:7; 84:11,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-31","title":"Psalms 18:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>86:8; De 32:31,39; 1Sa 2:2; 2Sa 22:32; Isa 45:5,21,22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-32","title":"Psalms 18:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>girdeth.The girdle was a necessary part of the eastern dress: It strengthened and supported the loins; served to confine the garments close to the body; and to tuck them in when journeying. The strength of God was to his soul what the girdle was to his body.</p>\n<p>28:7; 91:2; 93:1; Isa 45:5; 2Co 3:5 maketh. 2Sa 22:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-33","title":"Psalms 18:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>maketh. 2Sa 2:18 high. De 32:13; 33:29; 2Sa 22:14; Hab 3:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-34","title":"Psalms 18:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>teacheth. 144:1; 2Sa 22:36; Isa 28:6; 45:1 so that. 46:9; Jer 49:35; Ho 1:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-35","title":"Psalms 18:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>shield. 5:12; 28:7; De 33:29; 2Sa 22:36 right. 17:7; 45:3 gentleness. or, with thy meekness thou hast multiplied me. 45:4; Isa 40:11; 22:3; 2Co 10:1; Ga 5:22,23; Jas 3:17,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-36","title":"Psalms 18:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>enlarged. 4:1; Job 18:7; 36:16; Lu 12:50; 24:46-48 feet. Heb. ancles. 2Sa 22:37; Pr 4:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-37","title":"Psalms 18:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>3:7; 9:3; 35:2,5; 118:11,12; Nu 24:17-19; Isa 53:10-12; 63:1-6 Re 6:2; 19:19,20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-38","title":"Psalms 18:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>1Sa 17:49-51; 23:5; 30:17; 2Sa 5:1-25; 8:1-18; 10:1-19; 18:7,8 @ 2Sa 21:15-22 22:39</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-39","title":"Psalms 18:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>girded. 32; Eze 30:24,25 subdued. Heb. caused to bow. 66:3; 2Sa 22:40; 1Ch 22:18; Isa 45:14; 1Co 15:25-28; Eph 1:22 Php 3:21 necks. La 5:5 that. 34:21; 2Sa 22:41; Pr 8:36; Joh 15:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-41","title":"Psalms 18:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>2Sa 22:42,43; Job 35:12,13; Pr 1:28; Isa 1:15; 59:1,2; Jer 11:11 Jer 14:12; Eze 8:18; Ho 7:14; Mic 3:4; Zec 7:13; Lu 13:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-42","title":"Psalms 18:42","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":42,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":42},"content":"<p>beat. 50:22; 2Ki 13:7; Isa 41:2,15,16 cast. Isa 10:6; 25:10; Zec 10:5; Mal 4:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-43","title":"Psalms 18:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>from. 2Sa 2:9,10; 3:1; 5:1-7; Ac 5:31 made. 22:27,28; 108:9; 2Sa 5:1-25; 8:1-18; 10:1-19; 22:44-46 Isa 49:6,22,23; 52:15; Ro 15:12,18; Eph 1:22 a people. Isa 52:15; 55:5; Ho 1:10; Ro 16:26; 1Pe 2:10; Re 11:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-44","title":"Psalms 18:44","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":44,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":44},"content":"<p>As soon, etc. Heb. at the hearing of the ear. Ro 10:16,17 strangers. Heb. sons of the stranger. 66:3; 81:15; De 33:29; 2Sa 1:13; Isa 62:8; Eze 44:7; *marg: shall submit. or, yield feigned obedience. Heb. lie. 68:30; 81:15; 2Sa 22:44-46</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-45","title":"Psalms 18:45","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":45,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":45},"content":"<p>strangers. Isa 24:4; Mic 7:17; Jas 1:11 afraid. Re 6:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-46","title":"Psalms 18:46","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":46,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":46},"content":"<p>Lord. 2Sa 22:47; Jer 10:10; Joh 14:19; Re 1:18 blessed. 2; 42:9 the God. 25:5; 68:20; 79:9; Ex 15:2; Isa 12:2; Lu 1:47 exalted. 21:13; 57:5,11; 99:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-47","title":"Psalms 18:47","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":47,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":47},"content":"<p>avengeth. Heb. giveth avengements for me. De 32:35; 2Sa 22:48; Na 1:2; Ro 12:19 subdueth. or, destroyeth. 47:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-48","title":"Psalms 18:48","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":48,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":48},"content":"<p>liftest. 22:27-30; 59:1,2; 89:13; Php 2:9 violent man. Heb. man of violence. 7:16; 86:14; 140:1,4,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-49","title":"Psalms 18:49","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":49,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":49},"content":"<p>will I give thanks. or, confess. 14:7; 30:12; 72:18,19; 138:4; 2Sa 22:50,51; Ro 15:9; 1Ti 6:13 sing. 108:3; Mt 26:30; Ro 15:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-18-50","title":"Psalms 18:50","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":50,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":50},"content":"<p>Great. 2:6; 78:71,72; 89:3,4; 144:10; 1Sa 2:10; 16:1; Ac 2:34-36 Php 2:9-11 to his. 89:20-38; 132:10; 2Sa 7:13; 1Ch 17:11-14,27; Isa 9:6,7 Lu 1:31-33,69; Ro 1:3; 11:29; Ga 3:16</p>"}]}